        more: "The past continuous describes an action that was in progress around a past time: At eight o'clock I was having dinner. It combines with the past simple to show interruption: While I was cooking, the phone rang (the longer action in continuous, the shorter action in simple). The while clause usually carries the continuous verb; the when clause carries the simple verb. Time expressions like at that moment, while, as, all evening anchor the action in a period rather than a point.",
